WEBVTT

00:07.770 --> 00:10.830
Why must you punish yourself like that?

00:25.220 --> 00:28.550
I understand there have been some
changes in the pirates recently.

00:30.560 --> 00:31.720
The pirates?

00:32.290 --> 00:34.420
How much do you know about the pirates?

00:34.730 --> 00:38.390
How much? They're just pirates, aren't they?

00:38.770 --> 00:41.670
Those who dropped out of Logos,

00:41.670 --> 00:44.610
boat people from surrounding countries,

00:44.610 --> 00:47.480
those who tried to climb up from Revinus.

00:47.480 --> 00:50.310
All kinds of people with all different reasons...

00:51.350 --> 00:54.840
I hear that they're starting
to become more organized.

00:58.690 --> 01:01.360
So you're saying that they have a leader now?

01:01.360 --> 01:02.820
Probably.

01:02.920 --> 01:04.690
And one more thing.

01:05.890 --> 01:08.230
There was an eyewitness account.

01:08.230 --> 01:10.530
Among the ships that appeared
to belong to the pirates,

01:10.530 --> 01:13.230
there was a ship that looked just like the Ishin.

01:13.230 --> 01:14.220
The Ishin...

01:15.540 --> 01:17.970
That's a pretty interesting story, don't you think?

01:22.940 --> 01:36.310
Sora ni toketa hane o matoi tobitate tsubasa de

01:22.940 --> 01:29.550
Cloaked in feathers melted into the sky

01:29.550 --> 01:36.320
Take flight on wings

01:50.660 --> 01:53.830
Morokute nigai kajitsu no you ni

01:50.670 --> 01:53.840
Like fragile but bitter fruit

01:53.830 --> 01:57.040
Hito no kokoro o miryou suru no

01:53.840 --> 01:57.050
It fascinates people's hearts

01:57.040 --> 02:00.140
Togi sumasareta shiroi yubi de

01:57.050 --> 01:58.550
The shadow that manipulates

01:58.550 --> 02:00.150
With sharpened fingers gleaming white

02:00.140 --> 02:03.310
Ayatsuru kage wa chi no kaori

02:00.150 --> 02:03.320
Smells of blood

02:03.310 --> 02:16.310
Shizumi aseta kodou o yobi samasu shi no sasayaki

02:03.320 --> 02:09.760
The whisper of Death

02:09.760 --> 02:16.320
That awakens fading heartbeats

02:17.290 --> 02:23.660
Sora ni toketa hane o matoi

02:17.300 --> 02:23.670
Cloaked in feathers melted into the sky

02:23.660 --> 02:29.900
Tobitatsu no wa gin no tsubasa

02:23.670 --> 02:29.910
Silver wings take flight

02:29.900 --> 02:36.380
Fukai kaze ni tsume o tatete

02:29.910 --> 02:36.380
Become the power that tears at deep winds

02:36.380 --> 02:46.110
Kirisaku chikara to nare

02:36.380 --> 02:46.120
With poised claws

02:47.100 --> 02:50.350
Brought to you by
BiG-GuY Fansubbing

02:50.800 --> 02:54.820
Episode 3
Pirates

03:09.120 --> 03:11.290
This don't look good, Captain.

03:11.290 --> 03:15.950
If we don't do something, the prey we've been
waiting so long for will be stolen by the military!

03:16.290 --> 03:18.320
Don't panic.

03:19.190 --> 03:22.160
Let's just see what kind of skills they have, okay?

04:02.700 --> 04:04.700
Come on, open up!

04:08.310 --> 04:09.300
We're going.

04:20.360 --> 04:21.820
Are we turning around?

04:22.360 --> 04:24.760
The road is blocked ahead.

04:25.230 --> 04:29.100
While Joe is distracting them, we'll go through.

04:29.100 --> 04:30.590
Get down, Sana!

04:36.740 --> 04:38.670
Damn you idiots!

04:38.670 --> 04:40.730
I hope you guys get killed!

04:59.030 --> 05:00.460
Capture that truck!

05:07.770 --> 05:08.500
Jin!

05:42.270 --> 05:43.260
Pull back!

06:34.260 --> 06:36.090
That's one down!

06:36.990 --> 06:39.520
Looks like they're almost down over there too.

07:28.210 --> 07:30.510
Terminate! Force termination!

07:49.730 --> 07:52.330
He wasn't able to control it at all.

07:52.330 --> 07:53.820
At this rate...

07:54.370 --> 07:59.200
No matter how hard we try, will it be impossible
without a Phantom-level pilot?

08:00.840 --> 08:05.750
I'm telling you, there's no sense in creating
something only monsters like them can control!

08:06.080 --> 08:10.450
Dr. Nobuto's control device is a total black box,

08:10.450 --> 08:12.920
and is difficult to analyze from a
physical or engineering standpoint.

08:12.920 --> 08:15.860
The bottom line is that you're not able
to create one, right?

08:15.860 --> 08:20.600
Chief of Staff, perhaps this research
should be reexamined from the top down.

08:20.600 --> 08:22.700
We must continue with it.

08:22.700 --> 08:25.630
What if all of it were to get into Drake's hands?

08:26.500 --> 08:29.100
I don't know what kind of ideas
he's put in the director's head,

08:29.100 --> 08:32.040
but he even has his own research facility.

08:33.310 --> 08:35.280
Does Phantom know anything about
that piece of information?

08:35.280 --> 08:38.110
It's only a matter of time before they hear about it.

08:38.410 --> 08:40.480
Phantom is still the one that
has been given preference

08:40.480 --> 08:43.510
in carrying out the order to recapture Venus.

08:43.890 --> 08:45.350
It goes against my judgment, but...

08:45.350 --> 08:47.290
Exactly.

08:47.290 --> 08:48.960
Assuming the worst-case scenario,

08:48.960 --> 08:51.930
we must thoroughly grasp the know-how
of mass production.

08:51.930 --> 08:55.260
Just so we can stop Drake from doing
whatever he pleases.

08:55.430 --> 08:58.400
Outside there's Satsuma, and inside there's Drake.

08:58.400 --> 09:00.830
We have troubles from within and without.

09:02.870 --> 09:05.100
This is not something we should talk lightly about!

09:17.180 --> 09:18.410
Wow...

09:39.140 --> 09:41.570
He's crying? HIM?

09:54.660 --> 09:56.250
Oh, man...

10:08.670 --> 10:10.260
Hey, hey!

10:13.670 --> 10:16.040
That ship, where is it going?!

10:34.760 --> 10:36.230
Climb up!

10:36.860 --> 10:37.920
Sana.

10:45.840 --> 10:47.770
Come on, hurry up!

10:51.350 --> 10:53.250
Don't point your gun at her, you got that?!

10:53.250 --> 10:54.780
Bastard, you wanna die?!

10:54.780 --> 10:55.250
Jin!

10:55.250 --> 10:55.650
Cut it out!
Jin!

10:55.650 --> 10:56.410
Cut it out!

11:02.290 --> 11:03.690
Hijin!

11:04.190 --> 11:06.490
You'd better not treat them roughly.

11:06.490 --> 11:08.460
They're to be treated as our guests.

11:08.460 --> 11:10.400
That's the order.

11:11.570 --> 11:12.900
But!

11:12.900 --> 11:14.770
This is far enough.

11:14.770 --> 11:16.570
I'll take them from here.

11:21.040 --> 11:22.570
Sorry about that.

11:25.880 --> 11:27.780
Come. This way.

11:31.850 --> 11:33.850
You sure have your guard down.

11:33.850 --> 11:36.890
I'm sure you know the consequences
of starting something up

11:36.890 --> 11:38.920
in the middle of enemy territory, right?

11:41.030 --> 11:42.000
Come in!

11:45.200 --> 11:49.140
Oh, so you're the one who brought
them to me, Oryo!

11:50.270 --> 11:52.710
I'm tellin' you, it's not Oryo!

12:05.350 --> 12:07.550
What do you plan to do with us?

12:11.360 --> 12:13.920
I understand you've been taking care of Gora.

12:15.230 --> 12:17.870
He was actually useful for once.

12:17.870 --> 12:20.160
Was that something you arranged?

12:20.500 --> 12:23.640
He's pretty streetwise for a little kid.

12:23.640 --> 12:26.700
He'll find something interesting
and then try to sell it to me.

12:27.210 --> 12:29.540
And that's why he was trying to get the Gladiator?

12:30.110 --> 12:33.710
Well, I was just curious to see
who was transporting it.

12:33.710 --> 12:36.820
You don't look like an ordinary pirate to me.

12:36.820 --> 12:39.180
Just who are you?

12:41.890 --> 12:45.690
This ship belongs to the military, doesn't it?

12:45.990 --> 12:48.030
Not only that, it's new.

12:48.030 --> 12:50.760
Don't worry about such trivial matters.

12:51.100 --> 12:53.070
Come on, have a seat.

13:01.110 --> 13:02.540
How 'bout some chocolate?

13:06.510 --> 13:10.710
There's nothing bad in 'em!
It's not something you can get every day!

13:10.820 --> 13:12.410
It's really good, you know.

13:16.420 --> 13:18.720
Doesn't go too good with the squid legs though.

13:25.230 --> 13:27.170
Why don't you have one, Sana?

13:39.180 --> 13:43.210
So you're like the nice big brother, huh?

13:43.580 --> 13:47.150
Judging from that thing you were carrying,

13:47.150 --> 13:49.250
you must've been with Phantom, right?

13:52.730 --> 13:54.060
Interesting.

13:55.130 --> 13:57.930
No doubt about it, they're Joe's and Jin's.

13:57.930 --> 14:01.530
And apparently, the girl was also with them.

14:01.740 --> 14:03.140
So this was two days ago?

14:03.140 --> 14:06.240
We were busy with the nuclear power plant incident,

14:06.240 --> 14:08.070
and that's why they were late in reporting it to us.

14:08.610 --> 14:12.270
So that's how desperately they want
to keep Phantom out of the loop.

14:13.180 --> 14:14.310
Assemble the troops.

14:19.050 --> 14:21.520
It's amazing you don't get tired of that.

14:21.520 --> 14:24.920
Day in and day out, what could
you possibly be foretelling?

14:29.430 --> 14:31.230
The moon?

14:31.230 --> 14:32.530
What does it mean?

14:32.530 --> 14:36.660
A ship... Anxiety... And...

14:37.240 --> 14:38.310
Betrayal.

14:47.350 --> 14:49.320
Yes, this is Steve.

14:50.680 --> 14:52.250
I see.

14:52.250 --> 14:54.240
Is it the rebels again?

14:55.090 --> 14:58.490
Yes, they are definitely rebels.

14:58.490 --> 15:00.290
They've been found.

15:01.200 --> 15:03.760
The traitors from Phantom.

15:15.110 --> 15:17.580
Is there something on my face?

15:20.450 --> 15:23.380
You're wasting your time if you're
trying to find out my intentions.

15:23.650 --> 15:26.480
You're the one who's doing that.

15:27.760 --> 15:30.860
Don't be rude! Stop staring at Jin!

15:30.860 --> 15:34.790
Whoa! Aren't you a spunky one, little girl!

15:39.600 --> 15:40.470
Oryo!

15:40.470 --> 15:42.440
I told you, I'm not Oryo!

15:42.440 --> 15:45.500
Can you take this young lady
outside for a little while?

15:46.610 --> 15:47.970
Jin!

15:49.080 --> 15:50.840
It's okay.

15:52.380 --> 15:53.470
Let's go.

16:02.520 --> 16:04.350
Why did you have her leave?

16:05.330 --> 16:08.000
I don't approve of your monopoly.

16:08.000 --> 16:08.900
What?

16:08.900 --> 16:14.270
That armor isn't the only thing you're
transporting with kid gloves, is it?

16:14.800 --> 16:16.460
What are you talking about?

16:16.900 --> 16:18.710
Don't play dumb with me.

16:18.710 --> 16:20.870
You called her Sana, right?

16:20.870 --> 16:23.810
That girl... where did you get her?

16:33.850 --> 16:35.220
Miss Oryo?

16:35.220 --> 16:36.590
Hijin.

16:37.160 --> 16:38.290
Miss Hijin?

16:38.290 --> 16:39.060
What?

16:39.060 --> 16:42.130
Um, what about Jin?

16:42.130 --> 16:44.000
Don't worry.

16:44.000 --> 16:48.100
Toraji... The boss isn't such a bad guy.

16:48.100 --> 16:49.590
He's just a little strange, that's all.

16:49.770 --> 16:52.270
But he's a pirate, isn't he?

16:52.270 --> 16:53.870
He's a bad guy, right?

16:53.870 --> 16:55.930
Well, I guess you could say that.

16:57.750 --> 17:00.870
There are all kinds of pirates, you know.

17:02.580 --> 17:05.750
But it's weird. That kimono.

17:05.750 --> 17:07.320
He's wrapped it the wrong way.

17:07.320 --> 17:09.450
Oh yeah?

17:12.590 --> 17:14.260
You done talking?

17:14.260 --> 17:16.790
We can't see eye to eye on anything!

17:17.700 --> 17:19.970
He's more stubborn than he looks.

17:19.970 --> 17:21.870
I guess I have no choice.

17:21.870 --> 17:26.100
Missy, I hate to do this, but how about
I talk to you instead?

17:31.950 --> 17:35.140
H-hey, slow down a little!

17:39.350 --> 17:41.150
Which way, Gora?

17:44.390 --> 17:45.320
Gora!

17:50.900 --> 17:51.960
Ouch!

17:52.700 --> 17:54.930
Gora! Which way?

17:57.970 --> 17:59.940
Just to let you know,

17:59.940 --> 18:04.180
I'm not guaranteeing you that the ship
will definitely be there.

18:04.180 --> 18:08.080
It's just one of the harbors they stop at!

18:08.080 --> 18:09.950
This better not be another trick of yours!

18:11.720 --> 18:15.780
Trick you? How could you say such a terrible thing!

18:16.090 --> 18:19.290
I'm the one who was tricked...

18:19.290 --> 18:21.660
Those guys left without telling me.

18:21.660 --> 18:24.220
It ain't worth the trouble
if I can't even pick up my pay.

18:26.100 --> 18:27.590
Which way is it?

18:28.200 --> 18:29.800
Let me rest a little more!

18:29.800 --> 18:31.200
Which way?

18:37.310 --> 18:39.680
W-what do you want from me?

18:39.680 --> 18:42.880
You'd better not do anything weird or I'll scream!

18:43.150 --> 18:46.140
Unfortunately, I'm not into that.

18:47.020 --> 18:50.480
Missy. Can you just tell me one thing?

18:52.860 --> 18:55.350
You were on that airplane, weren't you?

20:43.970 --> 20:45.530
Everything's okay now.

20:45.970 --> 20:47.960
We're here to rescue you.

20:50.440 --> 20:52.810
Our target is Venus...

20:52.810 --> 20:54.620
Sana Nobuto.

20:54.620 --> 20:56.050
And the fugitive soldiers?

20:56.750 --> 20:58.270
Dispose of them.

21:02.360 --> 21:03.850
That's it.

21:04.860 --> 21:06.350
That island.

21:17.570 --> 21:20.540
So, the other one's here.

21:28.720 --> 21:30.180
How pathetic.

21:34.720 --> 21:37.760
Disposing of the traitors sounds
like a lot more fun to me.

21:37.760 --> 21:41.700
I'm sure you understand.
Our objective is to recapture Venus.

21:41.700 --> 21:43.390
That's our top priority.

21:45.870 --> 21:49.390
Yes. Things are moving along.

21:49.840 --> 21:52.270
I should be able to send you good news soon.

21:53.310 --> 21:55.080
All right. I understand.

21:55.080 --> 21:56.470
I'll keep in touch.

22:25.270 --> 22:29.780
Nagai kioku no hate ni

22:25.270 --> 22:29.740
If at the end of our long memory

22:29.740 --> 22:35.580
Time will tear us apart

22:29.780 --> 22:35.610
Toki ga bokura o wakatsu nara

22:37.620 --> 22:44.260
If at the end of my sweet memory with you

22:37.650 --> 22:44.290
Kimi to amai kioku no hate ni

22:44.260 --> 22:50.560
You and I become one again

22:44.290 --> 22:50.600
Mata bokura hitotsu nara

22:50.560 --> 22:57.740
From a quietly stretched arm's length away

22:50.600 --> 22:57.770
Sotto te nobashita kyori kara

22:57.740 --> 23:02.440
I will search for the meaning

22:57.770 --> 23:02.480
lmi o sagasu kara

23:02.440 --> 23:08.280
Can you hear it? The words dance in midair

23:02.480 --> 23:08.320
Kikoeru? Kotoba ga chuu ni mau

23:08.280 --> 23:14.090
We shall meet when our wish is granted

23:08.320 --> 23:14.120
Kanaeta toki ni deau

23:14.090 --> 23:17.760
Leaving only their reverse behind

23:14.120 --> 23:17.790
Reverse dake nokoshite

23:17.760 --> 23:21.160
The torn words

23:17.790 --> 23:21.190
Chigireta kotoba

23:21.160 --> 23:27.290
Blurred time and light

23:21.190 --> 23:27.330
Kasureta jikan to hikari

23:29.470 --> 23:33.800
I have found them now

23:29.500 --> 23:33.840
lma, mitsuketa kara

23:35.260 --> 23:46.860
<b><i>Next Episode</i></b>

23:44.280 --> 23:47.050
Next time on Innocent Venus:

23:47.820 --> 23:50.780
<b><i>Episode</i> <i>4
<b><i>Invasion</i></b></i></b>

23:48.260 --> 23:49.460
"Invasion"
